### AI features

- [AI features overview](https://www.metabase.com/docs/latest/ai/start)
- [Metabot](https://www.metabase.com/docs/latest/ai/metabot)
- [Metabot in Slack](https://www.metabase.com/docs/latest/ai/metabot-slack)
- [Agent API](https://www.metabase.com/docs/latest/ai/agent-api)
- [MCP server](https://www.metabase.com/docs/latest/ai/mcp): Model Context Protocol server for AI tool integration. Returns interactive charts inline in AI clients (Claude, Cursor, VS Code). Supports read and write: run SQL, update questions and dashboards, create collections.
- [File-based development](https://www.metabase.com/docs/latest/ai/file-based-development)
- [AI settings](https://www.metabase.com/docs/latest/ai/settings): configure AI features and enable or disable AI capabilities instance-wide. Power Metabot with your own provider — Anthropic, OpenAI, AWS Bedrock, or Azure — using your own key, including on open source, or let Metabase's AI service handle it (Cloud).
- [AI usage controls](https://www.metabase.com/docs/latest/ai/usage-controls): control which user groups can access Metabot, and set token and message limits per group.
- [AI customization](https://www.metabase.com/docs/latest/ai/customization): customize Metabot's name, icon, and illustrations for white-labeled deployments.
- [AI system prompts](https://www.metabase.com/docs/latest/ai/system-prompts): add standing instructions that shape Metabot's behavior across all tools.
- [AI usage auditing](https://www.metabase.com/docs/latest/ai/usage-auditing): pre-built admin dashboard tracking token spend, feature adoption, and user activity trends.

