- [Google Play + Metabase](https://www.metabase.com/integrations/google-play): store listing conversion, installs against uninstalls, and earnings from the Play Console bulk reports in Cloud Storage.

## Metrics

Definition, required data, SQL patterns, and pitfalls for the metrics these integrations power.

### Sales metrics

- [Win rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/win-rate): the share of deals that close won, why the denominator matters, and how to hold a cohort fixed.
- [Sales cycle length](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/sales-cycle-length): how long deals take to close, why it needs stage-change history, and why medians beat averages.
- [Pipeline coverage](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/pipeline-coverage): open pipeline divided by quota, and why the target is 1 ÷ win rate rather than a generic 3×.
- [Conversion rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/conversion-rate): overall and stage-to-stage funnel conversion, and why stage conversion requires stage history.
- [Average deal size](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/average-deal-size): typical won-deal value (ACV), and why the median matters more than the mean.
- [Reply rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/reply-rate): the share of contacted prospects who reply to outbound, why the denominator matters, and how to exclude auto-replies.
- [Meetings booked](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/meetings-booked): qualified meetings from outbound, booked vs. held, and how to avoid double-counting.
- [Forecast accuracy](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/forecast-accuracy): how close the forecast came to actuals, why you need snapshots, and how to track bias.
- [Email bounce rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/email-bounce-rate): the share of sent emails that fail to deliver, hard vs. soft bounces, and protecting deliverability.
- [Deal profitability](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/deal-profitability): margin per won deal from CRM and finance data joined, discount depth, and SQL to measure it in Metabase.
- [Deal slippage rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/deal-slippage-rate): committed deals whose close dates slip out of the period, why it needs snapshots, and SQL to measure it in Metabase.

### Revenue metrics

- [MRR (Monthly Recurring Revenue)](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/mrr): how to normalize plans to a monthly amount, MRR movement, and SQL to measure MRR and ARR in Metabase.
- [Churn rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/churn-rate): revenue vs. customer churn, voluntary vs. involuntary churn, and SQL to measure churn in Metabase.
- [Net revenue retention (NRR)](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/net-revenue-retention): NRR vs. gross retention, cohort-based measurement, and SQL to track NRR and GRR in Metabase.
- [LTV (Customer Lifetime Value)](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/ltv): estimating LTV from ARPU, churn, and gross margin, and how it feeds LTV:CAC in Metabase.
- [ARPU (Average Revenue Per User)](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/arpu): ARPU vs. ARPA, the right denominator, and SQL to measure average revenue per user or account in Metabase.
- [Failed-payment rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/failed-payment-rate): failed vs. attempted charges, dunning recovery, and SQL to measure involuntary churn in Metabase.

### Support metrics

- [First-response time](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/first-response-time): the wait for the first human reply, why to report the median and p90, and SQL to measure it in Metabase.
- [Resolution time](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/resolution-time): created-to-resolved time, whether to subtract pending time, and SQL to measure it in Metabase.
- [CSAT](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/csat): positive ratings over total ratings, why response rate matters, and SQL to track customer satisfaction in Metabase.
- [Ticket volume](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/ticket-volume): tickets created vs. solved, backlog by age, and SQL to measure support load in Metabase.
- [Cost per ticket](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/cost-per-ticket): fully-loaded support cost over tickets handled, by channel and tier, and SQL to measure it in Metabase.
- [Resolution rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/resolution-rate): the share of tickets that end resolved, reopens excluded, and SQL to measure it in Metabase.
- [Ticket backlog](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/ticket-backlog): open tickets trended daily with age buckets and created-vs-solved flow in Metabase.
- [Escalation rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/escalation-rate): escalated over total tickets by path and topic, and SQL to find documentation gaps in Metabase.
- [Deflection rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/deflection-rate): self-service resolutions over total demand with explicit signals, and SQL to measure it honestly in Metabase.
- [First contact resolution rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/first-contact-resolution-rate): tickets resolved in a single touch — strict vs. no-reopen definitions, and SQL to measure FCR in Metabase.
- [SLA breach rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/sla-breach-rate): tickets that missed first-response or resolution SLA targets by policy and priority, and SQL to track breaches in Metabase.

### E-commerce metrics

- [Average order value (AOV)](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/average-order-value): revenue per order net of discounts and refunds, why the median matters, and SQL to measure it in Metabase.
- [Repeat purchase rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/repeat-purchase-rate): the share of customers who buy again, why to cohort by first order, and SQL to measure retention in Metabase.
- [Refund rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/refund-rate): refunded revenue over revenue by order cohort, count vs. value rates, and SQL to measure it in Metabase.
- [Cart abandonment rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/cart-abandonment-rate): abandoned checkouts over started, cart vs. checkout stages, and SQL from event data in Metabase.
- [GMV (gross merchandise value)](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/gmv): total order value net of cancellations, GMV vs. revenue vs. take rate, and SQL to track it in Metabase.
- [Inventory turnover](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/inventory-turnover): COGS over average inventory from snapshots, days of inventory, and slow-mover SQL for Metabase.

### HR metrics

- [Time to hire](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/time-to-hire): candidate or application start to accepted offer, with p50 and p90 SQL patterns.
- [Time to fill](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/time-to-fill): requisition open to accepted offer or start date, measured at role grain.
- [Offer acceptance rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/offer-acceptance-rate): accepted offers divided by settled extended offers.
- [Candidate conversion rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/candidate-conversion-rate): stage-to-stage recruiting funnel conversion from ATS stage history.
- [Source quality](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/source-quality): source outcomes from applications through interviews, offers, and accepted hires.
- [Interview pass-through rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/interview-pass-through-rate): candidates advancing after completed interview stages.
- [Employee turnover rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/employee-turnover-rate): annualized departures over average headcount from HRIS snapshots, split voluntary vs. involuntary and by tenure.
- [Cost per hire](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/cost-per-hire): recruiting cost over hires by quarter and source, paired with 90-day retention as the quality gate.

### Finance metrics

- [Cash runway](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/cash-runway): available operating cash divided by average monthly net burn.
- [Accounts receivable aging](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/accounts-receivable-aging): open invoice balances grouped by days past due at a specific as-of date.
- [Days sales outstanding](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/days-sales-outstanding): average AR relative to credit sales and the number of days in the period.
- [Burn rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/burn-rate): gross operating cash outflow and net cash consumed after operating inflows.
- [Gross margin](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/gross-margin): revenue remaining after direct cost of revenue.
- [Budget variance](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/budget-variance): actual performance compared with one approved budget version.
- [Invoice collection rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/invoice-collection-rate): payments allocated to an invoice cohort divided by the amount invoiced.
- [FX exposure](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/fx-exposure): foreign-currency balances and commitments translated at a documented valuation rate.

### Work management metrics

- [Task completion rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/task-completion-rate): completed work divided by due or committed work, and why the denominator matters.
- [Task throughput](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/task-throughput): completed work per period, by project, team, or work type.
- [Overdue rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/overdue-rate): open work past due divided by open work with due dates.
- [Workload balance](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/workload-balance): open, overdue, and blocked work distribution across owners and teams.
- [Project health score](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/project-health-score): a transparent risk score from overdue, blocked, stale, and incomplete work.
- [Cycle time](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/cycle-time): started-to-done flow time for work items when status history is available.
- [Documentation freshness](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/documentation-freshness): active content reviewed or meaningfully updated inside its policy window.
- [Knowledge-base coverage](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/knowledge-base-coverage): required topics and workflows with current, owned documentation.
- [Workspace activity rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/workspace-activity-rate): eligible boards, spaces, sites, or channels with meaningful recent activity.
- [Collaboration response time](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/collaboration-response-time): time from a request or thread to its first useful human reply.
- [Knowledge-base health dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/knowledge-base-health): freshness, ownership, topic coverage, stale content, activity, and sharing risk across knowledge tools.

### Software delivery metrics

- [DORA metrics](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/dora): the four keys — deployment frequency, lead time for changes, change failure rate, and MTTR.
- [Deployment frequency](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/deployment-frequency): production deployments per period — a DORA throughput metric.
- [Lead time for changes](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/lead-time-for-changes): commit to running in production — a DORA throughput metric.
- [Change failure rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/change-failure-rate): the share of deployments that cause a failure — a DORA stability metric.
- [Build success rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/build-success-rate): successful CI runs over all completed runs, segmented by branch and pipeline.
- [Pipeline duration](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/pipeline-duration): median and p95 CI wall-clock time, with queue time tracked separately.
- [Flaky test rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/flaky-test-rate): tests that both pass and fail on the same code — the tax on every build.
- [Test pass rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/test-pass-rate): passing over executed test cases by suite — distinct from build success rate, with quarantine honesty.
- [Queue time](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/queue-time): how long work waits in kanban states and CI queues — usually the biggest share of lead time.
- [Release burndown](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/release-burndown): remaining scope vs. time with scope-added visible; needs snapshot or changelog history.
- [Velocity](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/velocity): points completed per sprint as a planning signal — never a cross-team productivity comparison.
- [Bug count](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/bug-count): net new bugs by severity and open-bug age buckets — the trends behind the raw total.

### Marketing metrics

- [ROAS](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/roas): conversion value over ad spend by campaign and channel, and why cross-platform comparisons are directional.
- [Customer acquisition cost (CAC)](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/cac): spend over new customers — blended vs. paid-only, and payback math.
- [Cost per lead](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/cost-per-lead): spend over leads, raw vs. qualified, so cheap channels don't hide bad leads.
- [Cost per click (CPC)](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/cost-per-click): the price of attention per channel, with CPM alongside.
- [Click-through rate (CTR)](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/click-through-rate): clicks over impressions or delivered emails — the denominator changes by context.
- [Landing-page conversion rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/landing-page-conversion-rate): conversions over sessions per landing page, with sample-size thresholds.
- [Organic clicks & impressions](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/organic-traffic): search visibility from Search Console — branded vs. non-branded, position, and CTR.
- [Activation rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/activation-rate): signups reaching the product's value moment, segmented by acquisition channel.
- [Sync success rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/sync-success-rate): successful pipeline runs over all runs per destination, with a row-weighted version for partial syncs.
- [Data freshness](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/data-freshness): time since the last successful delivery per destination — catches pipelines that go silent instead of failing.
- [Unsubscribe rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/unsubscribe-rate): opt-outs over delivered per campaign, read next to spam complaints, and SQL to localize spikes in Metabase.
- [List growth rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/list-growth-rate): net subscriber growth with components broken out, and cohort-quality SQL by acquisition source in Metabase.
- [Cost per acquisition (CPA)](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/cpa): spend over conversions, blended vs. per-channel, and why warehouse-deduplicated conversions beat platform-reported ones.
- [Bounce rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/bounce-rate): sessions with no engagement (GA4 definition), bounce vs. exit rate, and segmentation by landing page and source.
- [Net new leads](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/net-new-leads): leads created net of duplicates, junk, and disqualifications — the honest top-of-funnel volume metric.
- [Email open rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/open-rate): unique opens over delivered, and why Apple Mail Privacy Protection means clicks decide, not opens.
- [Paid channel performance dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/paid-channel-performance): spend, ROAS, and efficiency across ad platforms in one unioned model.
- [Ad spend pacing dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/ad-spend-pacing): month-to-date burn against budget, with projections.
- [Marketing funnel dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/marketing-funnel): visit to signup to customer, by channel and campaign.
- [Organic search performance dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/organic-search-performance): queries, pages, CTR by position, and branded vs. non-branded clicks.
- [Paid vs. organic dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/paid-vs-organic): the acquisition mix over time, from ad, analytics, and Search Console data.
- [Product retention dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/product-retention): activation, cohort retention, and which channels send users who stay.
- [Email engagement dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/email-engagement): campaign CTR, deliverability, automation performance, and list health.
- [CDP sync health dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/cdp-sync-health): sync success, event volume anomalies, freshness SLOs, and schema quality across the customer data stack.
- [Newsletter growth dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/newsletter-growth): net subscriber growth by source, engagement per post, referrals, and revenue per send.

### SEO metrics

- [Average position](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/average-position): volume-weighted mean search rank — and why GSC and rank trackers report different numbers.
- [Keywords in top 10](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/keywords-in-top-10): tracked keywords in positions 1–10 — the visibility count that survives averaging.
- [Domain rating](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/domain-rating): vendor link-authority scores, trended within one vendor's scale.
- [Referring domains](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/referring-domains): unique linking domains per snapshot — domains, not raw backlinks.
- [Backlink velocity](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/backlink-velocity): net new referring domains per week, gains minus losses.
- [Share of voice](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/share-of-voice): volume-weighted visibility share across a fixed keyword and competitor set.
- [Organic CTR](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/organic-ctr): clicks over impressions by position bucket, and how SERP features bend it.
- [Organic visibility overview dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/organic-visibility-overview): position buckets, weighted average position, and estimated traffic from tracked keywords.
- [Keyword rank tracking dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/keyword-rank-tracking): daily positions, movers, striking-distance keywords, and volatility.
- [Backlink growth dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/backlink-growth): referring domains, new vs. lost links, velocity, and authority trends.
- [Competitor share of voice dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/competitor-share-of-voice): weighted visibility share across a fixed competitor set, with market traffic context.
- [Technical SEO health dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/technical-seo-health): audit health scores and issue trends across crawls.
- [Content performance dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/content-performance): publishing cadence joined to traffic, engagement, and conversions per piece.

## Dashboards

Step-by-step guides to the cards, data, and SQL behind common dashboards, and how to build each one in Metabase.

- [Software delivery dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/software-delivery): throughput, cycle time, backlog, and quality from issue-tracker data.
- [Sprint & cycle health dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/sprint-health): committed vs. completed, spillover, scope change, and burndown.
- [DORA metrics dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/dora): deployment frequency, lead time for changes, change failure rate, and MTTR.
- [CI pipeline health dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/ci-pipeline-health): build success rate, duration percentiles, queue time, and flaky tests.
- [Code review health dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/code-review-health): PR cycle time, review latency, reviewer load, and stale pull requests.
- [Feature flag rollout dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/feature-flag-rollout): flag change activity, rollout progress, flag debt, and change safety.
- [Bug & quality dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/bug-quality): bugs created vs. resolved, backlog by severity, and escape rate.
- [MRR / ARR dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/mrr): recurring revenue and net-new MRR movement (new, expansion, contraction, churn).
- [Churn & retention dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/churn-retention): revenue and customer churn, gross/net retention, and voluntary vs. involuntary churn.
- [Subscription analytics dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/subscription-analytics): active base, plan mix, trials, and trial-to-paid conversion.
- [Failed payments dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/failed-payments): failed-payment rate, at-risk MRR, and dunning recovery.
- [Cohort retention dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/cohort-retention): revenue retention by signup cohort and LTV.
- [Support overview dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/support-overview): volume, first-response and resolution time, backlog, and CSAT.
- [Ticket volume dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/ticket-volume): created vs. solved, net flow, and backlog by age.
- [SLA & response-time dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/sla-response-time): SLA attainment, breaches, and aging of open work.
- [CSAT dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/csat): satisfaction trend, response rate, reopen rate, and drivers.
- [Agent performance dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/agent-performance): workload balance, resolution time, and CSAT by agent.
- [E-commerce sales dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/ecommerce-sales): net revenue, orders, AOV, and revenue by channel.
- [Conversion funnel dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/ecommerce-conversion-funnel): session-to-purchase steps and checkout drop-off.
- [Repeat purchase dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/repeat-purchase): repeat purchase rate, cohorts, and lifetime value.
- [Product performance dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/product-performance): best sellers, revenue by product, and return rate.
- [Win rate dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/win-rate): win rate by cohort, segment, source, and stage entered.
- [Lead funnel dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/lead-funnel): stage-to-stage conversion and funnel drop-off.
- [Sales forecast dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/sales-forecast): weighted vs. unweighted pipeline, commit vs. best-case, and coverage.

### Observability metrics

- [Incident count](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/incident-count): qualifying incidents per period, segmented by severity and service, and why the definition matters more than the number.
- [Mean time to acknowledge (MTTA)](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/mtta): created-to-acknowledged as a median — the paging-health half of incident response.
- [Error rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/error-rate): failed events over total requests, sessions, or users, and why the denominator decides everything.
- [Alert noise rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/alert-noise-rate): the share of alerts that never became incidents — the alert-fatigue early warning.
- [Service availability](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/service-availability): successful requests or minutes over total per service, request-based vs. time-based.
- [SLO compliance](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/slo-compliance): reliability against explicit targets — error budgets and burn rates.
- [Resource utilization](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/resource-utilization): used over requested or provisioned capacity — the bridge between reliability and cost.
- [Uptime](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/uptime): time-based availability from synthetic checks — nines as downtime budgets, maintenance-window rules.
- [MTBF](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/mtbf): mean time between failures, MTBF vs. MTTF, and the availability identity with MTTR.
- [Incident response dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/incident-response): incident volume, MTTA, MTTR, on-call load, and service reliability.
- [Alert quality dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/alert-quality): alert volume, alert-to-incident conversion, and the noisiest monitors.
- [Service availability dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/service-availability): availability, error rates, and latency percentiles by service.
- [SLO tracking dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/slo-tracking): error budgets, burn rates, compliance, and breach history.
- [Release quality dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/release-quality): error rates by release, regressions, and change failure rate.
- [Infrastructure cost dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/infrastructure-cost): utilization vs. requests, spend by service, and idle resources.

### Cloud cost metrics

- [Total cloud spend](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/total-cloud-spend): spend per period under one stated convention — amortized vs. unblended vs. net of credits.
- [Cost per customer](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/cost-per-customer): allocated infrastructure cost per customer, shared-cost distribution rules, and the revenue join for margin.
- [Cost growth rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/cost-growth-rate): month-over-month spend change, attributed to services and compared against business growth.
- [Commitment coverage rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/commitment-coverage-rate): commitment-covered share of eligible spend, and why it must be read with utilization.
- [Effective savings rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/effective-savings-rate): realized savings over on-demand-equivalent cost — the honest commitment-program health number.
- [Untagged spend rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/untagged-spend-rate): the share of spend nobody owns — the ceiling on every allocation dashboard.
- [Budget burn rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/budget-burn-rate): budget consumed vs. period elapsed, with forecast-to-exhaustion alerts.
- [Cost per service](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/cost-per-service): provider vs. application service cost, and the resource-to-service mapping.
- [Cloud spend overview dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/cloud-spend-overview): total spend, service and account breakdowns, growth, and budget burn.
- [Cost allocation by team and tag dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/cost-by-team-tag-allocation): ownership views with the untagged bucket visible.
- [Cost per customer dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/unit-economics-cost-per-customer): unit economics with revenue joined for margin per customer.
- [Commitment coverage dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/commitment-coverage): Savings Plans, RIs, and CUDs — coverage, utilization, and expirations.
- [Cost anomaly dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/cost-anomalies): spend spikes as an operational queue with deviations and response times.
- [Kubernetes cost dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/kubernetes-cost): namespace and workload cost with idle share and efficiency.
### Community metrics

- [Member growth rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/member-growth-rate): net new community members per period, with joins and departures reported separately.
- [Engagement rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/engagement-rate): the share of members active in a stated window, and why that window has to be published.
- [RSVP-to-attendance conversion](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/rsvp-to-attendance-conversion): registrations that became check-ins, and what it takes to measure attendance at all.
- [Active member rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/active-member-rate): active members over total members with a written activity definition, plus the 7d/30d stickiness ratio.
- [Member growth dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/member-growth): joins, departures, growth rate, and cohort retention of members.
- [Engagement activity dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/engagement-activity): posts, replies, reactions, active member ratio, and top contributors.
- [Event performance dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/event-performance): registrations, attendance conversion, ticket revenue, and repeat attendees.
- [Community health dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/community-health): answer rates, time to first response, and contributor concentration.

### Customer success metrics

- [Health score](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/health-score): composing an account health score from its parts instead of trusting a vendor black box.
- [Gross revenue retention](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/gross-revenue-retention): retained recurring revenue excluding expansion — the number that can never exceed 100%.
- [Renewal forecast accuracy](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/renewal-forecast-accuracy): forecast vs. actual renewals graded against a forecast frozen at period start.
- [Time to value](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/time-to-value): median time to a value milestone you have explicitly defined.
- [No-show rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/no-show-rate): booked meetings that never happened, with cancellations kept out of the denominator.
- [Renewal rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/renewal-rate): logo vs. gross renewal rate against contracts due, on-time vs. late, and the auto-renew split.
- [Expansion revenue rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/expansion-revenue-rate): expansion MRR over starting MRR — the growth component inside NRR, with contraction shown separately.
- [Customer health dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/customer-health): health distribution, risk tiers, score movers, and health vs. real product usage.
- [Renewal forecast dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/renewal-forecast): ARR up for renewal, forecast category mix, at-risk ARR, and forecast accuracy.

### Security metrics

- [Open critical vulnerabilities](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/open-critical-vulnerabilities): open critical and high findings, deduplicated across scanners, by asset group and age.
- [Mean time to remediate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/mean-time-to-remediate): median days from a finding's first-seen to resolved, by severity — not the incident-recovery MTTR.
- [Vulnerability SLA compliance](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/vulnerability-sla-compliance): findings closed within their severity SLA over all findings due, counting the overdue.
- [Mean time to detect (MTTD)](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/mttd): median time from first malicious activity to detection — a lower bound, honestly caveated.
- [Control pass rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/control-pass-rate): passing controls over monitored controls per compliance framework, from daily snapshots.
- [MFA adoption rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/mfa-adoption-rate): active users with a strong second factor enrolled, segmented by factor type and privilege.
- [Failed login rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/failed-login-rate): failed authentication attempts over all attempts — user friction separated from attack signal.
- [Scan coverage](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/scan-coverage): assets scanned or agent-protected within a window over the true inventory.
- [Vulnerability management dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/vulnerability-management): open exposure, remediation velocity, SLA compliance, and aging across scanners.
- [Incident response trends dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/incident-response-trends): detection volume, MTTD, triage speed, and false-positive rate for the SOC.
- [Compliance posture dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/compliance-posture): control pass rates by framework, failing controls, and audit readiness.
- [Identity & access analytics dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/identity-access-analytics): auth health, MFA adoption, threat signals, and lifecycle hygiene.
- [AppSec findings dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/appsec-findings): SAST, SCA, and bug-bounty findings across repos and programs.
- [Attack surface coverage dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/attack-surface-coverage): scan and sensor coverage against the true asset inventory.
### Product insights metrics

- [Net Promoter Score](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/nps): percent promoters minus percent detractors on the 0-10 scale — with sample-size rules and channel caveats.
- [Survey response rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/survey-response-rate): responses over invitations, opens, or views — and why the denominator must be labeled.
- [Survey completion rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/survey-completion-rate): completed over started responses, with drop-off-by-question analysis.
- [Feedback vote velocity](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/feedback-vote-velocity): new votes on open feature requests per period, not lifetime totals.
- [Time to close the loop](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/time-to-close-the-loop): median time from feature request to shipped and announced.
- [Feature adoption rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/feature-adoption-rate): adopting accounts over eligible active accounts, with tried vs. adopted tiers.
- [Rage-click rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/rage-click-rate): frustration clicks normalized per session, trended per page and release.
- [Voice of customer overview dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/voice-of-customer-overview): NPS, CSAT, top requests, and close-the-loop rate in one view.
- [Feature request pipeline dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/feature-request-pipeline): statuses, vote velocity, aging, and time to ship.
- [NPS & CSAT trends dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/nps-csat-trends): score trends with volume, segments, and verbatim themes.
- [Survey performance dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/survey-performance): response and completion rates and question drop-off.
- [Feature adoption & engagement dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/feature-adoption-engagement): adoption, breadth, activation, and declining accounts.
- [Session frustration signals dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/session-frustration-signals): rage clicks and friction by page, flow, and release.

### LLM analytics metrics

- [Token usage](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/token-usage): prompt and completion tokens per period by model and app, and why to track them separately.
- [Cost per 1M tokens](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/cost-per-1m-tokens): the blended LLM unit cost — the honest number for comparing models and catching drift.
- [LLM cost per user](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/llm-cost-per-user): LLM spend over active users of AI features — the unit-economics headline, with its skew.
- [p95 LLM latency](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/p95-llm-latency): the tail response time of LLM calls — percentiles over averages, and time-to-first-token for streaming.
- [LLM error rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/llm-error-rate): failed LLM calls over all calls — provider errors, timeouts, rate limits, and guardrail blocks separately.
- [Cache hit rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/cache-hit-rate): cached responses and tokens over totals — the most direct LLM cost and latency lever.
- [Eval pass rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/eval-pass-rate): passing eval examples over all examples — the test-suite green rate for LLM quality.
- [LLM requests per day](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/llm-requests-per-day): daily LLM call volume by app and model — the denominator behind every other LLM metric.
- [LLM spend overview dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/llm-spend-overview): daily spend, growth, cost per request, and budget tracking.
- [Model usage & cost dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/model-usage-cost): model mix, cost per 1M tokens, cache savings, and deprecated-model traffic.
- [LLM latency & errors dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/llm-latency-errors): latency percentiles, failure types, and retry rates.
- [LLM adoption & unit economics dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/llm-adoption-unit-economics): active users, cost per user, and retention splits.
- [Eval quality tracking dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/eval-quality-tracking): pass rates, regressions, model comparisons, and eval coverage.

### Commerce vertical metrics

- [Course completion rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/course-completion-rate): students finishing a course over those with time to finish, with the cohort maturity window and free-vs-paid segmentation that make it honest.
- [Platform fee rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/platform-fee-rate): the share of gross sales lost to platform commission, payment processing, and payout fees — derived from fee lines, not the vendor's rate card.
- [Shipping cost per order](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/shipping-cost-per-order): billed label cost per order and as a share of order value, using post-adjustment carrier charges with voided labels excluded.
- [On-time delivery rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/on-time-delivery-rate): deliveries arriving by the promised date over shipments with a known outcome, reported next to its tracking-coverage denominator.
- [Average check size](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/average-check-size): restaurant and retail average ticket, with voids excluded and comps, tax, and tips handled deliberately.
- [App store conversion rate](https://www.metabase.com/metrics/app-store-conversion-rate): product page views converted to first-time installs, and why Apple and Google define and name it differently.
- [Course revenue dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/course-revenue): gross vs. net revenue after platform and payment fees, product mix, refunds, and payout reconciliation.
- [Membership growth dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/membership-growth): active members, new vs. churned, revenue by tier, and churn by tenure cohort.
- [Shipping cost dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/shipping-cost): label spend, cost per order, carrier and zone cost drivers, and on-time delivery.
- [Restaurant & POS sales dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/restaurant-sales): net sales by location, average check, menu mix, discounts and voids, and tender mix.
- [App store performance dashboard](https://www.metabase.com/dashboards/app-store-performance): the impressions-to-installs funnel, proceeds after commission, and subscription movement.

